<title>UK: Key economic forecasts from UK budget.</title>
<headline>Key economic forecasts from UK budget.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the key short-term economic forecasts from the 1997/98 budget announced by Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke (percentage changes on a year earlier unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>								     FORECAST</p>
<p>						     1995	1996     1997</p>
<p>EXPENDITURE AT CONSTANT PRICES</p>
<p>Domestic demand				  1.5	 2.25     3.75</p>
<p>    Consumers' expenditure		   2.0	 3.0	4.25</p>
<p>    General govt. consumption		1.5	 1.0	0.75</p>
<p>    Fixed investment			  -0.25	3.0	6.25</p>
<p>    Change in stockbuilding		  0.0	-0.5	0.0</p>
<p>Exports of goods and services		7.75	6.25     5.75</p>
<p>Imports of goods and services		4.0	 7.0	6.75</p>
<p>GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT</p>
<p>Non-North Sea GDP				2.5	 2.5	3.5</p>
<p>Manufacturing output			   2.25	0.25     3.0</p>
<p>BALANCE OF PAYMENTS C/A</p>
<p> billion					 -4.0	-2.25    -4.25</p>
<p>percent of GDP				  -0.5	-0.25    -0.5</p>
<p>INFLATION</p>
<p>RPI ex-mortgage interest payments</p>
<p>(fourth quarter)				 3.0	 3.0	2.5</p>
<p>Producer output prices</p>
<p>(fourth quarter, excl fd,bev,tob,pet)    4.5	 0.75     1.0</p>
<p>GDP deflator at market prices</p>
<p>(financial year)				 2.5	 2.5	2.0</p>
<p>MONEY GDP AT MARKET PRICES</p>
<p>(FINANCIAL YEAR)</p>
<p> billion					  708	 746	787</p>
<p>percentage change				4.75	5.25     5.5</p>
<p>PSBR (FINANCIAL YEAR)</p>
<p> billion					  31.5	26.5     19.0</p>
<p>percent of GDP				   4.5	 3.5	2.5</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
